A||||2||ThatRickGuy||learning to drive a fiero.||||1||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||10-25-2000||08:58 AM||||Well, after owning the formula for like4 months I finally have a chance to learn how to drive it. Last night I headed out to the curviest road I know of, it's only a short drive off base, but it's always deserted, I was more parinoid about deer then people and cars. on the way out I was just pushing it a little, no to hard, and she held tight in all the corners, I was loving it. The way back, feeling a little more confident in the car and remebering the corners, I went a little faster. This is where I started to feel the slightly strange hadling characteristics. The front end never pushed out once (probrably due to my still slightly paranoid driveing, better to slow then in a tree) but on some of the corners, I could feel the weight shift on the rear end, and on one or two of the corners I actually felt the back end start to squeal and almost break loose. I just about jumped to the breaks, but just befor I pushed I rememebered that this wasn't my LeMans, and what everyone her said about hitting the gas, so I pulled my foot back over and began playing with the gas. car straightened out and held the rest of the corner great. IT's still going to take some getting used to, I just wanted to say thanks for the heads up on fiero driving!||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||10-25-2000||09:58 AM||||Give it a lot of gas halfway into the turns it should handle and feel great. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000002||Ed||10-25-2000||09:21 PM||||Recently there was another similar discussion about wet condition handling.<P>You've got to watch out for "dropped throttle oversteer" wherein you get off the gas in a corner and the rear end wants to come around. This is common with rear weight bias cars:  MR2, Fiat X1/9, Porsche ( especially 356's), etc.  <P>Road and Track, August 1985, has a very good discussion of this problem. (I've had Fieros since 1985, myself).  Check your library for past issues.<P>||||reg||1
